{"generated":"2026-06-22T14:42:30.328201+00:00","period_start":"2026-06-15T17:38:00+00:00","period_end":"2026-06-22T12:24:00+00:00","snapshot_count":28,"html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>The Vendetta Gazette – June 29, 1926</title>\n<style>\nbody { font-family: Georgia, serif; background: #f5ecd7; color: #1a1a1a; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }\nh1 { text-align: center; font-size: 2.8em; letter-spacing: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; border-top: 6px double #1a1a1a; border-bottom: 6px double #1a1a1a; padding: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 4px; }\nh2 { text-align: center; font-size: 1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 2px; margin-bottom: 16px; }\nh3 { font-size: 1.35em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a1a1a; margin-top: 24px; }\np { line-height: 1.75; margin: 10px 0; text-align: justify; }\nblockquote { background: #e8d9b5; border: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 20px 0; padding: 16px 20px; font-style: italic; }\nblockquote strong { display: block; font-style: normal; font-size: 1.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding-bottom: 4px; }\nhr { border: none; border-top: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 28px 0; }\n.subhead { font-style: italic; font-size: 1.05em; display: block; margin-top: -6px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: #444; }\n.byline { font-size: 0.85em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: #555; margin-bottom: 16px; display: block; }\n.leaderboard { background: #1a1a1a; color: #f5ecd7; padding: 12px 18px; margin: 16px 0; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }\n.leaderboard strong { display: block; text-align: center; font-size: 1.1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f5ecd7; padding-bottom: 4px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h1>The Vendetta Gazette</h1>\n<h2>Vol. XII &bull; June 29, 2026 &bull; &ldquo;All the Blood That&rsquo;s Fit to Print&rdquo; &bull; Two Cents (If You&rsquo;re Still Alive to Pay)</h2>\n\n<div class=\"leaderboard\">\n  <strong>&#9733; TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK &#9733;</strong>\n  Sir Caprice &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +83 turfs<br>\n  Donald Trump &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +20 turfs<br>\n  Free Willy &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +19 turfs<br>\n  haist24 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +3 turfs<br>\n  nhantris22 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +2 turfs<br>\n  Wu-Tang &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +2 turfs\n</div>\n\n<h3>The Annihilator Unchained — Again</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Sir Caprice Storms Ten More Headquarters; Vendetta City Runs Short of Bosses to Obliterate</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>Last week, dear reader, this correspondent exhausted the better part of his thesaurus endeavouring to describe the cataclysmic territorial rampage of one <strong>Sir Caprice</strong>. This week, your humble scribe is compelled to report — with a trembling hand and a generous tumbler of rye — that The Annihilator has done it again, and done it <em>worse</em>. Or better, depending upon which side of the tommy gun one finds oneself.</p>\n\n<p>In the seven days spanning this edition's reckoning, Sir Caprice has seized a staggering <strong>eighty-three turfs</strong>, battered down <strong>ten enemy headquarters</strong>, and simultaneously plundered the city's coffers through no fewer than forty-five lightning raids upon hapless rivals. His garrison, a fearsome private army already the envy of every two-bit racketeer from the waterfront to the gasworks district, has swelled by another two hundred and eleven souls — bringing his total fighting force to a positively terrifying <strong>six thousand, nine hundred and twelve gangsters</strong>. This is not an empire; it is a geological phenomenon. It is a landslide with a hat.</p>\n\n<p>Among the unfortunates who found their headquarters shattered beneath Sir Caprice's iron boot this week: the hapless <strong>Fahwa</strong>, the ill-starred <strong>Hossein Nftdan</strong>, the bewildered <strong>tẻtre</strong>, the twice-ruined <strong>Devkalio2</strong> — who had the singular misfortune of losing his newly re-established headquarters <em>twice in the same afternoon</em> — and the formerly respectable <strong>Merlin</strong>, whose garrison has now been reduced to a round and melancholy zero. When a man's garrison reads naught, gentlemen, he is not repositioning. He is broken.</p>\n\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"248\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Caprice</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+83</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"262\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+20</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"257\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+19</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">haist24</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"180\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+3</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">nhantris22</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"9\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"175\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+2</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wu-Tang</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"175\" width=\"9\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"175\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+2</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">THEHOH</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"203\" width=\"4\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"170\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+1</text>\n</svg>\n\n\n<h3>Donald Trump and Free Willy: The Ambitious Lieutenants</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Two Rising Powers Carve Their Own Bloody Paths Through the City's Weaker Precincts</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>While Sir Caprice commands the front page by divine right of sheer destructive volume, it would be a disservice to overlook the vigorous ambitions of <strong>Donald Trump</strong> and <strong>Free Willy</strong>, both of whom have enjoyed exceedingly productive weeks by any normal measure of criminal achievement.</p>\n\n<p>Trump — whose garrison now stands at a robust six thousand, four hundred and seventy-eight, swollen by one hundred and twenty-one fresh recruits — added twenty turfs to his portfolio and personally stormed two enemy headquarters. His most celebrated conquest was the <strong>demolition of Wcrypto's command post</strong>, a turf that the beleaguered Wcrypto had apparently failed to adequately garrison despite losing it — along with twenty other properties and nineteen raids upon his coffers — in a week so calamitous it defies polite description. Wcrypto, formerly among the city's more conspicuous operators, has been stripped to the bone.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Free Willy</strong>, meanwhile, proved himself a scrapper of genuine distinction, storming three headquarters — those of <strong>Garydark</strong>, the mysterious <strong>675vc</strong>, and the unfortunate <strong>321dasq</strong> — while adding nineteen turfs to his holdings. One notes with some amusement that Free Willy's garrison of sixty-eight men is, by the standards of this city's titans, positively microscopic. That a fellow commanding sixty-eight souls can storm three headquarters in a week suggests that Free Willy is either extraordinarily bold, extraordinarily lucky, or extraordinarily good at picking his moments. Possibly all three.</p>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"276\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HEAVIEST LOSSES THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wcrypto</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-20</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Duchess</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"320\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"486\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-16</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Azur Knights</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"240\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"406\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-12</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Garydark</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"386\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-11</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Ekmu</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"200\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"366\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-10</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Merlin </text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"175\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"266\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-5</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">FIFTH BLOOD EMPEROR</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"203\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"206\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-2</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Devkalio2</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"231\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"186\" y=\"244\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n</svg>\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"143\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HQ RAIDS — TOP ATTACKERS</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"148\" y=\"53\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Caprice</text>\n<polygon points=\"156,43 161,48 156,53 151,48\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\"/>\n<rect x=\"170\" y=\"41\" width=\"410\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#6b1010\" opacity=\"0.9\" rx=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"577\" y=\"41\" width=\"3\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#c03030\"/>\n<text x=\"588\" y=\"53\" fill=\"#c04040\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">10✕</text>\n<text x=\"148\" y=\"82\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<polygon points=\"156,72 161,77 156,82 151,77\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\"/>\n<rect x=\"170\" y=\"70\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#6b1010\" opacity=\"0.9\" rx=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"290\" y=\"70\" width=\"3\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#c03030\"/>\n<text x=\"301\" y=\"82\" fill=\"#c04040\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">3✕</text>\n<text x=\"148\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<polygon points=\"156,101 161,106 156,111 151,106\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\"/>\n<rect x=\"170\" y=\"99\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#6b1010\" opacity=\"0.9\" rx=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"249\" y=\"99\" width=\"3\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#c03030\"/>\n<text x=\"260\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#c0404